 "transcript": [
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung looks at his sons and then at the land.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son returns home.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We have come, father, with the spring in our hearts and we will not be idle.\"",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We will help you, father, with the spring planting and we will not be idle.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung forgets his sons' presence.",
  "[action] The eldest son follows his father as he works.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"It is only earth and it must be turned.\"",
  "[action] The eldest son turns earth.",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son talks with his father about the fields.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Now, father, we must not turn all the land to rice, for it is not good for the land to grow rice year after year. We must have a little millet and a little beans that we may eat them and have some money in hand. And we must have a little wheat that we may have bread and sell some to the townspeople.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"It is your land,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"do as you will with it.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung leaves",
  "[says] The eldest son discusses his plans with his brother.",
  "[says] (to the second son) The eldest son discusses his plans with his brother.",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"We will sell the land near the river and we will sell it to a rich man who will put up a wall and grow rice and we will have the money and we will buy another house that is larger and finer and we will be the first family in the town.\"",
